Škoda Auto Deutschland says access to the stored shop data was possible in principle but its logs cannot show whether or how much was copied, and it reported the incident to the data-protection authority without stating any 72-hour timing. Only the German accessories shop was affected, not other Škoda shops, the manufacturer's systems or Škoda Connect, and full card data is not stored in the shop; Škoda's advice to customers is to change reused passwords and watch for phishing that refers to their orders.
